# skybeta-06: make EKF2 accept this airframe's slow camera chain (see ../../DEBUG_TAKEOFF.md).
#
# Measured with the organisers' tools/latency_probe.py on skybeta-06, 2026-11-08:
#   image -> bridge publish  p50 219 ms (03:21 boot), 290 ms (03:00 boot); organisers' bench Orin: 70 ms.
# EKF2 fuses a vision sample of age A only if  A + EKF2_EV_DELAY < max(EKF2_DELAY_MAX, EKF2_EV_DELAY) + 100 ms
# (PX4 RingBuffer::pop_first_older_than 100 ms window), so with the fleet values 70 / 200 anything older
# than ~240 ms is silently dropped -> no local position -> Position mode falls back to Altitude ->
# flight_interface refuses Offboard -> PX4 position failsafe disarms on the ground.
#
# Organisers' rule (fleet_guide.md section 7, host/run.sh banner): "EKF2_EV_DELAY = measured, not assumed".
# This file sets it to the measured p50 and widens the buffer so samples up to ~350 ms old still fuse.
#
# Load: QGC -> Vehicle Setup -> Parameters -> Tools -> Load from file -> this file -> reboot the FC.
# Verify in the stack:  ros2 topic echo --once /fmu/out/estimator_status_flags | grep -E "cs_ev_(pos|yaw)"
#                       (both true)  and  /skybeta/state "local_enu" non-null, "nav_state_name" POSCTL
#                       with the RC switch on Position while disarmed.
# Revert: EKF2_EV_DELAY 70, EKF2_DELAY_MAX 200 (the fleet 03b_ekf2_vision.params values).
#
# Vehicle-Id	Component-Id	Name	Value	Type
1	1	EKF2_EV_DELAY	250.000000	9
1	1	EKF2_DELAY_MAX	500.000000	9
